<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Number System Guide</title>
    <style>
        body {
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            background: #f5f0ff;
            padding: 25px;
        }
        .container {
            max-width: 850px;
            margin: auto;
            background: white;
            padding: 25px;
            border-radius: 16px;
        }
        h1 { text-align: center; color: #7042b8; }
        table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; }
        th, td {
            padding: 14px;
            border: 1px solid #ccc;
            text-align: left;
        }
        th { background: #eee5ff; }
        .example {
            background: #f5f0ff;
            padding: 18px;
            margin-top: 20px;
            border-radius: 12px;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="container">
    <h1>🔢 Number Systems</h1>
    <p>Number systems represent numbers using different sets of digits.</p>

    <table>
        <tr><th>System</th><th>Base</th><th>Digits</th></tr>
        <tr><td>Binary</td><td>2</td><td>0, 1</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Octal</td><td>8</td><td>0–7</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Decimal</td><td>10</td><td>0–9</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Hexadecimal</td><td>16</td><td>0–9, A–F</td></tr>
    </table>

    <div class="example">
        <h2>Example</h2>
        <p>Decimal 10 = Binary 1010</p>
        <p>Decimal 15 = Hexadecimal F</p>
        <p>Binary numbers are widely used in digital computers.</p>
    </div>
</div>
</body>
</html>
